B.Y3=new A.an("feature_sleep","Sleep","[Action] Make a Ranged Attack vs Cha. On success target up to {Source} enemies range 6, and knock them prone and asleep. On the start of their turn, make a status check vs Wis. On success, they are stunned and remain asleep. Otherwise the effect ends for the target and they take their turn as normal. When sleeping, if an enemy is attacked or takes damage they wake up and the effect ends. An ally can spend an [Action] or [Reaction] to wake an ally.\n\n[Reaction] when an enemy is knocked prone, spend your reaction and make a status check vs Cha. On success, put the target and all prone enemies to sleep. If it is the target's turn, immediately make the status check as if it was the start of their turn.",B.L,B.abs,!1)
B.SZ=new A.t("feature_silence_voice_thief","Voice Thief","While Concentrating, Enemies range {Source} of you who are allies with one of the targets are creeped out by you using their voice. While in range, you and your allies gain a +1 to Int, Wis, Cha attack results against those enemies and +1 to Int, Wis, Cha Defense results from attacks caused by the enemies.")
B.U7=new A.t("feature_silence_sore_throat","Sore Throat","While concentrating, At the Start of your turn, gain 1d6 Sore Throat dice then roll your sore throat dice dealing that much damage to all targets. You may gain a max of {Source} sore throat dice.")
B.UV=new A.t("feature_silence_frustrating","Frustrating","While concentrating, Targets get a -1 to all skill and attack checks that do not include you as a target.")
B.abQ=s([B.SZ,B.U7,B.UV],t.U)
B.XH=new A.an("feature_silence","Silence","[Action] Make a Ranged Attack vs Int targeting Enemies in a {Half Source} space radius range 6/12. On Success, the targets are Silenced for as long as you remain concentrating. While silenced, they may not activate combat features, but can otherwise take their turn. If player characters gain this effect they cannot speak and must mime. If playing over voice only, they may only make noises. Chumps cannot trigger their chump actions.\n\n[Reaction] When you succeed on an attack, spend your reaction and start concentrating on silence targeting the triggering attack\u2019s targets. ",B.L,B.abQ,!1)
B.Wy=new A.t("feature_spirit_disruptive_spirit","Disruptive Spirit","Spaces adjacent to your spirit are difficult terrain for enemies. You and your allies have a +1 to attacks and status checks against enemies adjacent to your spirit. This doesn't include your spirit attacks. ")
B.Ux=new A.t("feature_spirit_horrifying_spirit","Horrifying Spirit","When an enemy starts range {Half Source} of your spirit, Make an Status Check vs Wis, On Success, Deal {Half Source d6} damage.")
B.WN=new A.t("feature_spirit_soothing_spirit","Soothing Spirit","When your allies start their turn within 1 of the spirit or enters within 1 of the spirit for the first time during their turn, they gain {half Source d6} shield.")
B.a9r=s([B.Wy,B.Ux,B.WN],t.U)
B.XJ=new A.an("feature_spirit","Spirit","[Action] Target an unoccupied square within 6 spaces, and summon your Spirit. As long as you remain concentrating, When you use the ability and as a [Reaction] on following turns, you may move your spirit Companion up to 6 spaces ignoring Difficult terrain, and make a Melee Attack vs Wis targeting enemies range 1. On Success Deal {Source d10} Damage ignoring shields and resistance. \n\nYour Spirit can be anything as long but takes up the space of a medium creature. It uses your defenses when attacked, and you take half of all damage that would be dealt to the spirit. This damage cannot be reduced in any way. You do not make concentration checks from damage to your companion. Allies and the spirit may flank.\n\n[Reaction] During your turn, spend your reaction and summon your spirit in an unoccupied space within 6\n",B.L,B.a9r,!1)
